------Iterating over a map--------

const map=new Map();
map.put(1,1);
map.put(2,1);
map.put(3,1);

using higher order loop
-------
  for(const key of map){
    console.log(key);
  }
  --along with key
  1.2
  for(const [key,value] of map){
    console.log(key);
  }
======

but we can't do the same for object like 1.2
For object we can do as like
  for(const key of object){
    console.log(key);
  }
  and for printing the values 
  --you can access it through the key of the object
    console.log(object[key]);
===


